rs from  what one can tell is i mean it was  basically part of a much bigger polling  operation in which they were sending out  emails at random to a database of uh  people whose email addresses they have  and also uh tell it bringing telephone  numbers outline them to a database of  telephone numbers stay hard so this is  less in the way of pre-selected people  um part of you know just part of the  general public but in the course of that  picked up  800 people who said they were  conservative members so it's a different  methodology  two companies have produced not  dissimilar results of their estimates  and both intentions of the public in  general over recent months but they're  clearly diverged in this case i think  all one can say is that you know  technique is a new company and maybe  they're right or maybe they're wrong  ugov's record of um leadership polls is  a pretty good one they were virtually  spot on in their estimates of the  proportion of labour party members that  we're going to vote for jeremy corbyn in  2015 and 2016 they were pretty much spot  on in the battle between cameron and  david davis in 2005 though they were a  little bit high  on boris johnson's score in the 2019  contest equally opinion who are the  other company who've done this in the  past and they're promising us  i know the poll next week they've got a  pretty good record indeed they've got  the boris johnson versus jeremy hunt  contest almost down to a single point so  it's a difficult thing to do we are  trying to get hold of a very specialist  section of the population they represent  less than one percent of the population  but one has to say  given their record in the past one  certainly cannot ignore  what comes out from the companies  that  have been doing this on a regular basis  and i guess the worrying thing for the  sunup camp is that  it's not just that the you know new  government showing this trust well ahead  um as indeed our conservative home with  their  survey o